'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... isp_hub75_morphMask.spin2
''   Purpose.... Coverage masks of a digit's stroke pieces: a round pen, anti-aliased, flat or tube cross-section
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Oct 2026
''   Updated.... 13 Oct 2026
''   Version.... v1.0.0
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ A digit is the 2021 figure drawn with a round pen of thickness T (spec R-4.3): straight runs on the
  figure's centre lines, quarter-circle joints at its corners, round free ends. A group builds the
  masks of its pieces once, when it is placed, into one buffer; every digit of the group draws through
  them (isp_hub75_morph7seg), reading each mask as it is, transposed or mirrored:

      straight  the pen drawn along a centre line of segLength - T pixels: a capsule, T rows of
                straightColumns() columns. The seven segments' straight runs.
      join      the same capsule with a centre line of T + 1 pixels: the run that joins a side's upper
                and lower segments where both are lit.
      arc       a quarter circle of centre-line radius ARC_RADIUS = (T + 1) / 2, its centre at the
                mask's bottom-right pixel centre, bending from the left of the mask to its top: the
                figure's top-left corner. At stroke 1 its corner pixel is THIN_CORNER_LEVEL (by eye). Every corner and every place the middle segment meets a side
                is this arc, mirrored. Its inner edge has a radius of half a pixel at every thickness.
      dot       a disc of the colon dot's size, centred in its square.

  Every mask is row-major, one byte per pixel: BYTE[pMask][row * nCols + col], 0 = not covered ...
  COVER_FULL = fully covered at full brightness. Rows run across a capsule and columns along it.

  Where the pieces sit. With P = segLength + 1 (the 2021 spacing of the centre lines), the figure's
  centre lines are x = T/2 and T/2 + P, y = T/2, T/2 + P and T/2 + 2P, so a straight edge always lies on
  a pixel edge. A capsule's centre line starts T/2 pixels into its mask, plus half a pixel when T is
  even (capsulePhase()): that is where the figure puts every straight run's start.

  Coverage. Each byte is clamp(T/2 + 1/2 - d, 0, 1), d the distance from the pixel's centre to the
  piece's centre line (a pixel centred on the pen's edge is half lit): exact on a straight edge that lies
  on a pixel edge, and smooth around the curves. Pieces overlap where they meet; the renderer keeps the
  brighter of two pieces there, so their union is one stroke with no seam.

  Cross-section (spec R-4.4). Flat: a covered pixel is lit by its coverage. Tube: also weighted by
  1 - (1 - TUBE_EDGE_LEVEL) x (d / (T/2))^2, so the pen's edge is TUBE_EDGE_LEVEL of its centre, scaled
  so a pixel on the centre line (or nearest to it) is fully lit.

  This object has no state: it fills the caller's buffer and keeps nothing.
}

CON ' stroke settings

  ' cross-section (spec R-4.4)
  '   SECTION_FLAT - even brightness across the stroke
  '   SECTION_TUBE - brightest along the centre line
  #0, SECTION_FLAT, SECTION_TUBE

  MIN_THICKNESS = 1                                             ' the thinnest stroke, in pixels
  COVER_FULL = 255                                              ' a fully covered pixel at full brightness

  THIN_CORNER_LEVEL = 64                                        ' stroke 1: the corner pixel the arc passes through, lit at about a
                                                                '   quarter (Stephen, 2026-10-14, by eye: its coverage, 0.59, read too bright)
  TUBE_EDGE_LEVEL = 0.4                                         ' tube: brightness at the edge, as a fraction of the centre (float; chosen by eye, spec R-4.5)

CON ' geometry

  JOIN_EXTRA = 1                                                ' a join's centre line is the stroke plus this: twice the arc radius
  CENTER_DIVISOR = 2                                            ' half of a thickness (integer)
  LAST_OFFSET = 1                                               ' the last index of a count is the count minus this

CON ' float constants (Spin2 float operators take float operands)

  F_NONE = 0.0                                                  ' no distance, no coverage
  F_HALF = 0.5                                                  ' half a pixel: a pixel's centre; the pen's edge is half lit
  F_ONE = 1.0                                                   ' full coverage; full weight
  F_HALVES = 2.0                                                ' half of a length (float)

OBJ

    morphStatus : "isp_hub75_morphStatus"

PUB null()
'' This is not a top level object
''

PUB validateSection(crossSection) : status
'' Check a cross-section setting.
''
'' @param crossSection - SECTION_FLAT or SECTION_TUBE
'' @returns status - morphStatus.SUCCESS or E_UNKNOWN_CROSS_SECTION

    status := morphStatus.SUCCESS
    if crossSection <> SECTION_FLAT and crossSection <> SECTION_TUBE
        status := morphStatus.E_UNKNOWN_CROSS_SECTION

PUB capsulePhase(thickness) : phase
'' The whole pixels a capsule's mask adds for a half-pixel start: 1 when the thickness is even, else 0.
''
'' @param thickness - the stroke, in pixels
'' @returns phase - 0 or 1

    phase := (thickness + LAST_OFFSET) // CENTER_DIVISOR

PUB straightColumns(thickness, segLength) : nCols
'' The straight mask's columns: a centre line of segLength - thickness (the stroke at most segLength), the pen's
'' half at each end, and the phase.
''
'' @param thickness - the stroke, in pixels
'' @param segLength - the segment length, in pixels
'' @returns nCols - its columns (it has thickness rows)

    nCols := segLength + capsulePhase(thickness)

PUB joinColumns(thickness) : nCols
'' The join mask's columns: a centre line of thickness + JOIN_EXTRA, the pen's half at each end, and the phase.
''
'' @param thickness - the stroke, in pixels
'' @returns nCols - its columns (it has thickness rows)

    nCols := CENTER_DIVISOR * thickness + JOIN_EXTRA + capsulePhase(thickness)

PUB arcSide(thickness) : side
'' The arc mask's side: it is square.
''
'' @param thickness - the stroke, in pixels
'' @returns side - its rows and columns

    side := thickness + LAST_OFFSET

PUB joinOffset(thickness, segLength) : offset
'' Where the join mask starts in the figure's buffer.

    offset := thickness * straightColumns(thickness, segLength)

PUB arcOffset(thickness, segLength) : offset
'' Where the arc mask starts in the figure's buffer.

    offset := joinOffset(thickness, segLength) + thickness * joinColumns(thickness)

PUB dotOffset(thickness, segLength) : offset
'' Where the dot mask starts in the figure's buffer.

    offset := arcOffset(thickness, segLength) + arcSide(thickness) * arcSide(thickness)

PUB figureBytes(thickness, segLength, dotSize) : nBytes
'' The bytes buildFigure() needs: the straight, join, arc and dot masks, one after another.
''
'' @param thickness - the stroke, in pixels
'' @param segLength - the segment length, in pixels
'' @param dotSize - the colon dot's side, in pixels
'' @returns nBytes - the buffer size

    nBytes := dotOffset(thickness, segLength) + dotSize * dotSize

PUB buildFigure(pMask, maskCapacity, thickness, segLength, dotSize, crossSection) : status
'' Fill the masks of one digit figure: straight, join, arc and dot, one after another (see the offsets above).
'' The stroke runs from MIN_THICKNESS up to segLength, and the dot is MIN_THICKNESS or more. A refused request
'' writes nothing.
''
'' @param pMask - hub address of the caller's buffer: maskCapacity bytes
'' @param maskCapacity - size of that buffer in bytes
'' @param thickness - the stroke, in pixels
'' @param segLength - the segment length, in pixels
'' @param dotSize - the colon dot's side, in pixels
'' @param crossSection - SECTION_FLAT or SECTION_TUBE
'' @returns status - morphStatus.SUCCESS, or E_BAD_THICKNESS, E_THICKNESS_TOO_LARGE, E_UNKNOWN_CROSS_SECTION or
''   E_MASK_TOO_LARGE, with nothing written

    status := validateSection(crossSection)
    if thickness < MIN_THICKNESS or dotSize < MIN_THICKNESS
        status := morphStatus.E_BAD_THICKNESS
    elseif thickness > segLength
        status := morphStatus.E_THICKNESS_TOO_LARGE
    elseif status == morphStatus.SUCCESS and figureBytes(thickness, segLength, dotSize) > maskCapacity
        status := morphStatus.E_MASK_TOO_LARGE

    if status == morphStatus.SUCCESS
        buildCapsule(pMask, thickness, segLength - thickness, capsulePhase(thickness), crossSection)
        buildCapsule(pMask + joinOffset(thickness, segLength), thickness, thickness + JOIN_EXTRA, capsulePhase(thickness), crossSection)
        buildArc(pMask + arcOffset(thickness, segLength), thickness, crossSection)
        buildCapsule(pMask + dotOffset(thickness, segLength), dotSize, 0, 0, crossSection)

PRI buildCapsule(pMask, thickness, centreLength, phase, crossSection) | nCols, row, col, fHalfT, fStart, fEnd, fX, fY, fAlong, fMaxWeight
' The pen drawn along a centre line of centreLength pixels: thickness rows, centreLength + thickness + phase
' columns. The centre line runs at y = T/2 from x = T/2 + phase / 2.

' Local Variables:
' @local nCols - the mask's columns
' @local row, col - the pixel being filled
' @local fHalfT - half the thickness (float)
' @local fStart, fEnd - the centre line's ends along x (float)
' @local fX, fY - the pixel's centre (float)
' @local fAlong - the nearest point of the centre line to the pixel's centre, along x (float)
' @local fMaxWeight - the weight of the pixel nearest the centre line (float)

    nCols := centreLength + thickness + phase
    fHalfT := float(thickness) /. F_HALVES
    fStart := fHalfT +. float(phase) /. F_HALVES
    fEnd := fStart +. float(centreLength)
    fMaxWeight := tubeWeight(nearestCentre(thickness), fHalfT, crossSection)
    repeat row from 0 to thickness - LAST_OFFSET
        fY := float(row) +. F_HALF
        repeat col from 0 to nCols - LAST_OFFSET
            fX := float(col) +. F_HALF
            fAlong := fMax(fStart, fMin(fEnd, fX))
            BYTE[pMask][row * nCols + col] := coverByte(distance(fX -. fAlong, fY -. fHalfT), fHalfT, crossSection, fMaxWeight)

PRI buildArc(pMask, thickness, crossSection) | side, row, col, fHalfT, fCentre, fRadius, fX, fY, fDistance, fMaxWeight
' The top-left corner: a quarter circle of centre-line radius (T + 1) / 2, its centre on the centre of the
' mask's bottom-right pixel, from its left end (pointing down) to its top end (pointing right); round ends.

' Local Variables:
' @local side - the mask's rows and columns
' @local row, col - the pixel being filled
' @local fHalfT - half the thickness (float)
' @local fCentre - the circle's centre, in x and in y (float)
' @local fRadius - the centre line's radius (float)
' @local fX, fY - the pixel's centre, from the circle's centre (float)
' @local fDistance - from the pixel's centre to the centre line (float)
' @local fMaxWeight - the weight of the pixel nearest the centre line (float)

    side := arcSide(thickness)
    fHalfT := float(thickness) /. F_HALVES
    fCentre := float(thickness) +. F_HALF
    fRadius := float(thickness + LAST_OFFSET) /. F_HALVES
    fMaxWeight := tubeWeight(nearestCentre(thickness), fHalfT, crossSection)
    repeat row from 0 to side - LAST_OFFSET
        fY := float(row) +. F_HALF -. fCentre
        repeat col from 0 to side - LAST_OFFSET
            fX := float(col) +. F_HALF -. fCentre
            if fX <=. F_NONE and fY <=. F_NONE                     ' within the quarter: the distance from the circle
                fDistance := fabs(distance(fX, fY) -. fRadius)
            else                                                ' past an end: the distance from the nearer end
                fDistance := fMin(distance(fX +. fRadius, fY), distance(fX, fY +. fRadius))
            BYTE[pMask][row * side + col] := coverByte(fDistance, fHalfT, crossSection, fMaxWeight)
    if thickness == MIN_THICKNESS                               ' a 1-pixel corner: the 2021 diagonal step, its corner dimmed
        BYTE[pMask][0] := THIN_CORNER_LEVEL

PRI nearestCentre(thickness) : fDistance
' How far the pixel centres nearest a straight centre line are from it: 0 (odd thickness) or half a pixel (even).

    fDistance := (thickness // CENTER_DIVISOR == 0) ? F_HALF : F_NONE

PRI coverByte(fDistance, fHalfT, crossSection, fMaxWeight) : level | fCover
' A pixel's byte: its coverage at this distance from the centre line, times the cross-section's weight there.

' Local Variables:
' @local fCover - the pixel's coverage, 0.0 to 1.0 (float)

    fCover := fMax(F_NONE, fMin(F_ONE, fHalfT +. F_HALF -. fDistance))
    level := round(float(COVER_FULL) *. fCover *. tubeWeight(fMin(fDistance, fHalfT), fHalfT, crossSection) /. fMaxWeight) <# COVER_FULL

PRI tubeWeight(fDistance, fHalfT, crossSection) : fWeight | fRatio
' The cross-section's weight at this distance from the centre line: 1.0 for flat (float).

' Local Variables:
' @local fRatio - the distance as a fraction of the pen's half-width (float)

    fWeight := F_ONE
    if crossSection == SECTION_TUBE
        fRatio := fDistance /. fHalfT
        fWeight := F_ONE -. (F_ONE -. TUBE_EDGE_LEVEL) *. fRatio *. fRatio

PRI distance(fX, fY) : fLength
' The length of the vector (fX, fY) (float).

    fLength := fsqrt(fX *. fX +. fY *. fY)

PRI fMin(fA, fB) : fLower
' The lower of two floats.

    fLower := fA <. fB ? fA : fB

PRI fMax(fA, fB) : fHigher
' The higher of two floats.

    fHigher := fA >. fB ? fA : fB

CON ' license

